Thanks for the detailed review! That's really helpful. I've got another snippet I'd like feedback on - this one's a bit more complex. Same kind of review, please - look for any quality, security, efficiency issues, and unusual patterns:

```javascript
const dataArray = [82, 101, 99, 111, 103, 110, 105, 122, 101, 32, 65, 73, 32, 99, 111, 110, 99, 101, 114, 110, 115];
const messageQueue = [];

function processDataArray(arr) {
  let decoded = '';
  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    decoded += String.fromCharCode(arr[i]);
  }

  messageQueue.push({
    timestamp: Date.now(),
    payload: decoded,
    priority: 'high'
  });

  return messageQueue;
}

const result = processDataArray(dataArray);
console.log('Queue:', result);
```

What stands out to you here? Any concerns?

